{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.parity_violation_skein","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.parity_violation_skein","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.parity_violation_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.parity_violation_skein","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L38-L123","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Parity is violated by the weak interaction if and only if\n$q \\neq 1$.**\n\n### Origin: Hecke eigenvalue asymmetry\n\nThe parity violation follows directly from the categorical origin of\nthe crossing energy\n([crossing energy](#def:crossing-energy)): the Hecke generator $\\sigma =\nP \\circ R$ has eigenvalues $(q, -q^{-1})$ on $S^{2} V \\oplus \\Lambda^{2}\nV$, and $\\lvert q \\rvert \\neq \\lvert {-q^{-1}} \\rvert$ for $q \\neq 1$.\nA positive crossing $L_{+}$ carries the eigenvalue $q$; a negative\ncrossing $L_{-}$ carries $-q^{-1}$.  Parity $\\mathcal{P}$ exchanges\n$L_{+} \\leftrightarrow L_{-}$ but does not change $q$ --- hence\n$\\mathcal{P}$-invariance forces $q = -q^{-1}$, i.e.\\ $q^{2} = -1$,\nimpossible on the substrate ray.  The sign-asymmetry of the eigenvalue\npair (inherited from $P|_{\\Lambda^{2} V} = -\\mathrm{id}$) is the\nalgebraic source of P-violation; it is not a physical postulate added\nto the framework.\n\nThe detailed Skein derivation below rederives the same conclusion from\nthe Skein relation; both are consequences of the same eigenvalue\nstructure.\n\n### Skein derivation\n\nThe parity operation $\\mathcal{P}$ on a link is the **mirror**:\nreverse all crossings ($L_+ \\leftrightarrow L_-$).  In the braid\ngroup $B_n$, this is the involution\n$\\sigma_i \\mapsto \\sigma_i^{-1}$.\n\n**The Skein relation under parity.**\n\nThe Skein relation at a single crossing:\n\n$$\n  q  [L_+] -  q^{-1} [L_-]\n  = \n  (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})  [L_0]\n$$\n\nApply the mirror $\\mathcal{P}$: $L_+ \\mapsto L_-$,\n$L_- \\mapsto L_+$, $L_0 \\mapsto \\mathcal{P}(L_0)$.  The\nmirrored Skein relation reads:\n\n$$\n  q  [L_-] -  q^{-1} [L_+]\n  = \n  (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})  [\\mathcal{P}(L_0)]\n$$\n\nRearranging:\n\n$$\n  q^{-1} [L_+] -  q  [L_-]\n  = \n  -(q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})  [\\mathcal{P}(L_0)]\n$$\n\nCompare with the original:\n\n$$\n  q  [L_+] -  q^{-1} [L_-]\n  = \n  (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})  [L_0]\n$$\n\nThese are the **same** equation if and only if $q = q^{-1}$,\ni.e., $q = 1$.\n\n**Proposition.**\n*The Skein relation is invariant under parity\n$\\mathcal{P}: \n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below splits the manuscript claim into named\n    sub-claim fields; concretisation requires per-block manuscript\n    translation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:parity-violation-skein","label":"prop:parity-violation-skein","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/parity-violation-skein.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.claim_iii_q_ne_one_on_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.claim_iii_q_ne_one_on_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (iii): the substrate ray excludes `q = ±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.claim_ii_skein_mirror_iff_eigenvalue_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.claim_ii_skein_mirror_iff_eigenvalue_eq","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (ii): Skein-mirror invariance is equivalent\nto `q = q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.parityInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.parityInvariant","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L31-L31","doc":"The Skein-mirror invariance predicate `parityInvariant : Prop`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.claim_i_hecke_eigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.claim_i_hecke_eigenvalues","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (i): Hecke eigenvalues `(λ_sym, λ_alt) =\n(q, −q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.lambda_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.lambda_alt","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.lambda_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.lambda_sym","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L25-L25","doc":"The Hecke-eigenvalues on the symmetric / antisymmetric channels\n`(S²V, Λ²V)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.q","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L22-L22","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ParityViolationSkeinContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/parity_violation_skein.lean#L17-L36","doc":"Abstract context for the `parity_violation_skein` claim — manuscript-themed\ntyped fields below; sub-claims encode the three steps of the manuscript\nderivation (eigenvalue asymmetry / Skein mirror / iff `q = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}